    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d169">

                <pb facs="0172" n="98" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg98"/>

                <head>Mr. Burnley to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-03-15"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 15, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Sir</hi>: Would you permit me to recall your
                    attention to my note of the 28th January, enclosing copies of despatches
                    elucidatory of Earl Russell’s slave trade despatch, No. 9, of which I left you a
                    copy, relative to the joint invitation to powers declaring slave trade
                    piracy.</p>
                <p>Believe me to remain, my dear sir, yours, very faithfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. HUME BURNLEY.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
